Keep one ticket per supported cause. The old subject-only rule from
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merged different causes in 4471.
[Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) proposes its replacement.

1. Deduplicate export rows by report ID.
2. Read the body and look up the tenant's locale and booking-form version.
3. Use channel and tenant date order to distinguish the shared parser from the booking-v3 hint.
4. Merge only reports supported by the same cause. Subjects and browser-derived intake tags are clues.
5. Investigate unknown tenants and bodies that disagree with the cause assignment. Keep their counts explicit.
6. Refresh the data and regenerate counts before each handoff; the desk continues taking reports.

<DedupeExplorer />

See the [4471 review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) for the two groups, the uncertain reports
and the difference between report arrival and merge activity.

